ng_hci: tell ng_l2cap about ACL links created through the RAW hook

bluetoothd creates its ACL links itself, with Create_Connection on the
HCI RAW socket. con_compl() then finds no connection descriptor, makes
one, and sends LP_ConnectCfm to nobody: NG_HCI_CON_NOTIFY_ACL is set
only by an LP_ConnectReq. ng_l2cap learns the handle only when something
first opens a channel on the link (its LP_ConnectReq is answered at once
for an open link). Anything for the handle before that is dropped:

  ng_l2cap_lp_receive: ubt0l2cap - unexpected ACL data packet.
      Connection does not exist, con_handle=256
  ng_l2cap_lp_enc_change: ubt0l2cap - unexpected LP_Enc Change Event.
      Connection does not exist, con_handle=256

Beats Studio Pro send L2CAP signalling (an Information Request) as soon
as the link is up, often before bluetoothd opens its first channel; with
that request never answered they leave every channel this side opens
unanswered, so hands-free, AVRCP and A2DP all time out.

Set NG_HCI_CON_NOTIFY_ACL on a RAW-created ACL descriptor, so
ng_hci_lp_con_cfm() sends ng_l2cap LP_ConnectCfm before any ACL data or
Encryption_Change for the handle (the same hook and node queue, so in
order). NgL2cap's 0005 takes that unrequested LP_ConnectCfm as an open
link.

Also: encryption_change() passed a NULL descriptor to
ng_hci_lp_enc_change() for a handle it doesn't know (it logged the
invalid handle first, then dereferenced it). Skip the notification then.

Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd#666). Not upstream.
Applies to: releng/15.1 sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_evnt.c,
after 0008.

--- a/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_evnt.c
+++ b/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_evnt.c
@@ -821,6 +821,18 @@
 		}
 
 		bcopy(&ep->bdaddr, &con->bdaddr, sizeof(con->bdaddr));
+
+		/*
+		 * NextBSD: an ACL link created through the RAW hook (bluetoothd
+		 * sends Create_Connection itself) must reach ng_l2cap too. The
+		 * remote side can send L2CAP signalling, and the controller an
+		 * Encryption_Change, before anything opens a channel on the
+		 * link; until then ng_l2cap does not know the handle and drops
+		 * both. Send it LP_ConnectCfm now, ahead of anything else for
+		 * this handle (nextbsd/nextbsd#666).
+		 */
+		if (ep->link_type == NG_HCI_LINK_ACL)
+			con->flags |= NG_HCI_CON_NOTIFY_ACL;
 	} else if ((error = ng_hci_con_untimeout(con)) != 0)
 			goto out;
 
@@ -1072,7 +1084,9 @@
 			__func__, NG_NODE_NAME(unit->node), ep->status);
 
 	/*Anyway, propagete encryption status to upper layer*/
-	ng_hci_lp_enc_change(con, con->encryption_mode);
+	/* NextBSD: not for a handle we do not know (nextbsd/nextbsd#666) */
+	if (con != NULL)
+		ng_hci_lp_enc_change(con, con->encryption_mode);
 
 	NG_FREE_M(event);
 
